===Etymology===
From {{proto|Germanic|fulkan|people|lang=ang}}, from ''*fulka-'' ‘crowd, army’.  Cognate with Old Frisian [[folk]], Old Saxon ''folc'', Old Dutch ''folk'' (Dutch [[volk]]), Old High German ''folc'' (German [[Volk]]), Old Norse [[folk]] ‘people, army’, Related to Latin ''[[vulgar]]/[[vulgus]]''

